      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Harnessing robust **quantum entanglement** is fundamental to transitioning from theoretical models to scalable, fault-tolerant quantum processors. Demonstrating strong violations of the **Bell inequality** experimentally validates the existence of true **non-locality**, which is the resource powering advanced quantum computation. Maintaining high **qubit coherence** while enabling long-distance **entanglement distribution** is key to achieving genuine quantum advantage and realizing the threshold for **quantum supremacy**. This foundational work directly supports the development of secure **entanglement-based cryptography**, offering transformative security paradigms for future networks.",
      "source": "target",
